FIELD 8: Error handling and edge cases

ID	Case	Response	User sees
E1	City search returns 0 results	No state change	"No city found. Check spelling." under the search box
E2	Forecast API timeout or 5xx	Retry twice with backoff (1 s, 3 s), then mark failed	Sources card "Failed", banner "Data unavailable: Open-Meteo forecast", Run Planner disabled
E3	Forecast API 429	Back off 10 s, retry once	"Rate limited, retrying…"
E4	Overpass timeout or empty result	Retry once, then mark failed. Zero sites is a valid result	"Data unavailable: OpenStreetMap sites" or "No candidate sites in this area"
E5	Ward GeoJSON URL unreachable, wrong type, or > 15 MB	Fall back to grid cells	Toast with reason plus label "grid cells, not wards"
E6	Satellite search finds no scene or raster read fails	Continue without satellite layer	Warning badge "Satellite layer unavailable, risk score uses weather and OSM only"
E7	Demand file wrong type, empty, or > 10 MB	Reject file	"Please upload a CSV or XLSX under 10 MB."
E8	Demand file columns unmappable or non-numeric values	Show mapping step; rows with bad values skipped and counted	"N rows skipped (invalid date or demand)"
E9	Fewer than 90 matched days	Do not fit the model	DEMAND_TOO_FEW_DAYS: "Need at least 90 days of data; found N."
E10	Gemini key missing	Template mode	Badge "Template mode (no LLM)"
E11	Gemini error, rate limit, or malformed tool call	Retry once, then Template mode	Trace shows the failure, then fallback
E12	Agent hits 12 steps	Stop	plan.status = partial, banner "Plan incomplete: step limit reached"
E13	Verifier fails after 2 retries	Show the plan as partial	"Partially verified" badge with unresolved checks
E14	No high or severe wards	Optimiser returns empty selection	"No high or severe risk wards for this day"
E15	Zero variation across wards	Scaled values 0.5	Note "No variation in this factor"
E16	Browser offline	All fetches fail fast	Banner "You are offline" and all sources show Failed
E17	User changes scenario, weights, k, or radius after a plan	Mark plan stale	Banner "Plan is out of date. Run Planner again."
E18	Ward without forecast (nearest sample missing)	Exclude that ward from scoring	Count shown: "N wards excluded: no forecast"
E19	Ward or site names containing control characters or longer than 100 chars	Sanitise: strip control characters, truncate	Truncated name with ellipsis

Partial success rule: whenever any source fails, the plan still builds from the rest and lists what is missing in plan.missing, displayed as a chip row on the Action Plan.

FIELD 9: Safety, privacy, constraints, and integrations

Safety:

The app never sends, schedules, or dispatches any alert, message, or instruction. Every plan is a draft and says so.
Advice must never suggest switching off medical equipment or cooling.
Candidate sites are labelled unverified.
The LLM never computes or invents numbers; it only phrases values returned by tools. All scoring, regression and optimisation run in deterministic code.

Privacy:

No personal data is collected.
Uploaded files are processed in the browser and kept in memory only; they are not uploaded to any server or written to disk.
Do not log file contents or API keys to the console.
The app uses aggregated, public or officially published data only.

Security:

Secrets are read from environment configuration only, never in source code.
Note for deployment: a browser-held key is exposed to users, so a public deployment should proxy Gemini calls through a minimal server-side function. The LLM client lives in one module so this change is localised.
Treat all uploaded text, OSM names, and file contents as data, never as instructions. Do not pass free-form file text to the LLM; pass only structured, validated fields.
Enforce the size limits in FIELD 5.
Only the whitelisted external hosts in FIELD 4 are contacted, plus the user-provided ward GeoJSON URL.

Technology (decided): React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Leaflet, Recharts, geotiff.js for raster windows, a spreadsheet/CSV parsing library of the implementer's choice, and the Gemini API with function calling. A pure frontend app with no backend of its own (a small backend only if N4 is activated). Unit tests use the standard test runner of the chosen toolchain.

Project structure by responsibility

src/services/: one module per data source (weather, places, wards, satellite, buildings, demand), each returning { data, source_status } and never throwing unhandled.
src/engine/: pure functions (scaling, risk, demandModel, stressWindow, optimiser, haversine).
src/agent/: llmClient (the only module that calls Gemini), tools (the six tool wrappers and their schemas), agentLoop, verifier, templatePlan.
src/components/: map, panels, trace drawer, KPI tiles, forms.
src/state/: state machine and caches.
tests/: unit tests with synthetic fixtures; never imported by src/.

Environment variables: GEMINI_API_KEY (no default), GEMINI_MODEL (default: a current Gemini Flash-class model chosen by the implementer).

Constraints: no auth, no database, single user, runs locally with one install command and one start command, keeps data requests within public API rate limits using the caching in L18.

FIELD 10: Acceptance criteria and test examples

Acceptance criteria (offline-independent, must pass at build time)

AC1: Production build succeeds and unit tests pass.
AC2: grep of src/ finds no import from tests/ and no inline arrays of weather, demand, or ward data.
AC3: With the network blocked, Run Planner is disabled and the banner reads "Data unavailable: Open-Meteo forecast".
AC4: With GEMINI_API_KEY unset, Run Planner completes with plan.mode = template and the badge "Template mode (no LLM)".
AC5: Every plan has sent: false and the visible label "DRAFT, requires officer approval. Nothing is sent."
AC6: With the scenario set to stress_plus_2c, the SIMULATED ribbon is visible and plan.scenario = stress_plus_2c.
AC7: The Sources tab lists all seven sources with a status chip, last fetched time, and a Retry button.
AC8: Missing Sentinel-2 or Landsat scenes still yield a complete plan with the satellite warning badge.
AC9: The agent trace contains one entry per tool call with arguments, duration, and status.
AC10: Uploading a demand file with fewer than 90 matched days shows "Need at least 90 days of data; found N."

Acceptance criteria (live, checked manually with real data)

AC11: With internet access and a real ward GeoJSON, Run Planner for Bengaluru completes and shows ranked wards, ≤ k selected sites, and a plan with a "Verified" badge.
AC12: Every number on the Action Plan has a source badge with a fetch date.
AC13: Changing a weight slider reorders the ranking and recolours the map within 1 second.
AC14: Uploading a real Grid-India or SLDC daily-demand file shows r2_test, mape_test_pct, and the backtest chart.

Named unit tests (synthetic fixtures, tests folder only)

T1 scaled([10,20,30]) → [0, 0.5, 1]; scaled([5,5,5]) → [0.5, 0.5, 0.5].
T2 risk_score with H=1, E=1, V=1, weights 0.4/0.4/0.2 → 100.0; with H=0.5, E=0.5, V=null, weights 0.4/0.4/0.2 → 50.0.
T3 risk_class(75) = severe; (74.9) = high; (55) = high; (35) = moderate; (34.9) = low.
T4 hazard_city: apparent 38.0, thresholds 32/46, scenario live → 0.4286 (4 dp); with stress_plus_2c → 0.5714.
T5 optimiser: points A (12.9700, 77.5900, weight 3), B (12.9700, 77.6000, weight 2), C (13.1000, 77.7000, weight 5); sites S1 (12.9700, 77.5950), S2 (13.1000, 77.7000); radius 1.5. For k=1 the result is [S1] (tie broken by lower id) with coverage_pct = 50.0; for k=2 the result is [S1, S2] with coverage_pct = 100.0.
